claim.claim-text:
a) providing a fermented beverage solution comprising an acidic congener, preferably an organic acid, and more preferably acetic acid;
b) treating the fermented beverage solution by adding an alkaline treating agent to the fermented beverage solution to neutralize at least a portion of the acidic congener to a salt, preferably to an organic salt, and more preferably to an acetate salt; and
c) removing at least a portion, or all, of the neutralized acidic congener from the treated fermented beverage solution, thereby producing a refined fermented beverage having a reduced or negligible concentration of the acidic congener, preferably acetic acid, relative to the fermented beverage solution.

(i) providing a batch of the fermented beverage solution comprising the acidic congener;
(ii) extracting a sample of the fermented beverage solution from the batch;
(iii) titrating the sample with an alkaline treating agent to neutralize at least a portion of the acidic congener within the sample to form a salt;
(iv) calculating the amount of the salt formed by the titration of alkaline treating agent into the sample;
(v) determining a quantity of alkaline treating agent to add to the batch, based on the titration of alkaline treating agent into the sample; and
(vi) adding the determined quantity of alkaline treating agent to the batch to neutralize at least a portion of the acidic congener within the batch and form a salt;
wherein the alkaline treating agent used to treat the fermented beverage solution is either the same alkaline treating agent used to titrate the sample, or is a different alkaline treating agent in a stoichiometric-equivalent quantity.

(i) a pH in the range of 5.5 to 8.5, preferably 5.8 to 6.5;
(ii) at least 10%, and up to 20%, by volume, ethyl alcohol;
(iii) a combined concentration of acetic acid and acetate less than 1000 ppm, preferably in a range of 300 ppm to 400 ppm, and
(iv) a concentration of acetic acid less than 500 ppm, preferably in a range of 10 ppm to 100 ppm, and more preferably in a range of 25 ppm to 75 ppm.

(i) a pH in the range of 5.5 to 8.5, preferably 5.8 to 6.5;
(ii) at least 10%, and up to 20%, by volume, ethyl alcohol; and
(iii) a combined concentration of acetic acid and acetate less than 1000 ppm.
